.* RUNBCKUP: the task menu that runs a backup.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='RUNBCKUP'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.F1=Help
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION='CMD CALL QCMD'.F9=Command line
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=RUNBCKUP HELP=HLPRUNBCKUP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Run Backup
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.To select one of the following, type its number below and press Enter:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD RUNBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*DAILY)'.Run daily backup
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD RUNBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*WEEKLY)'.Run weekly backup
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD RUNBCKUP BCKUPOPT(*MONTHLY)'.Run monthly backup
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD QSMNSAVE OPTION(21)'.Back up the entire system
:EMENU.
:BOTINST.Type a menu option below
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPRUNBCKUP.Run Backup - Help
:P.Options 1 to 3 run a backup now with the options set up for it (GO
BACKUP option 10). Option 11 saves the whole system the way GO SAVE
option 21 does.
:P.Type an option number and press Enter. F9 opens a command line, F3
leaves the menu and F12 returns to the one before it.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
